# `yo fix <path> --module-names` (plans/backlog/KEBAB_CASE_NAMES.md Part C,
# VERDICTS-67): `check` first warns once per project-local module file or
# directory whose name is not kebab-case. `--dry-run` prints the rename map and
# touches nothing; the run renames the files and directories (a file, a
# directory, a directory module with an `index.yo` and an upper-case name) and
# rewrites what resolves to them: a relative import with and without `.yo`,
# `../`, a `[modules]` key and value (`demo/string_util`), a path under the
# package root (`demo/deep_dir/thing`) and the `build.yo` root. A std import
# outside the paths stays as written. The second run renames nothing, and the
# renamed project checks without a warning.
check src/main_app.yo
fix . --module-names --dry-run
fix . --module-names
fix . --module-names
check src/main-app.yo
